# Secret Tunnel: "can't be blocked this turn" (CR 611.2a, 514.2). Bot1 makes the Captain and the Protectors unblockable on turn 5
# and doesn't attack; on turn 7 the flag is gone and Bot2's Ornithopter blocks the Protectors.

[Bot1 Deck]
Secret Tunnel
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Water Tribe Captain
Earth Kingdom Protectors
Island
Mox Emerald
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Secret Tunnel.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Water Tribe Captain.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Earth Kingdom Protectors.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Secret Tunnel.Activate(Ability: share)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Water Tribe Captain; Bot1.Battlefield.Earth Kingdom Protectors)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Earth Kingdom Protectors.CantBeBlocked = true
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Earth Kingdom Protectors.CantBeBlocked = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Earth Kingdom Protectors > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Earth Kingdom Protectors)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
